+## Tauri mode
+
+The desktop app is moving to Tauri (epic #3517). A Tauri release has no WebDriver, so a repro of
+the Tauri app runs on a **CI artifact of the commit under test**, not on an installed release.
+The Electron workflow below stays valid for Electron releases until Step 43 (#3560).
+
+1. **Build the artifact.** The PR's own run of `desktop-tauri-ci.yml` already uploads it. For
+   another ref: `gh workflow run desktop-tauri-ci.yml --ref <ref>`, then
+   `gh run list --workflow desktop-tauri-ci.yml -L 1` for the run id. Artifacts:
+   `memry-tauri-e2e-windows-arm64` and `memry-tauri-e2e-linux-arm64` (driven by WebDriver), and
+   the `debug` twins (no driver, for startup checks). They expire after 14 days.
+2. **Fresh VM.** `winvm.sh new` or `linvm.sh new`, as in the Electron workflow.
+3. **Install.** `winvm.sh install-artifact <run-id> [--variant e2e|debug]` copies
+   `memry-tauri.exe` to `C:\Users\agent\memry-tauri\` and prints the WebView2 Runtime version.
+   `linvm.sh install-artifact <run-id>` installs `libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 libsoup-3.0-0
+   libayatana-appindicator3-1 libsecret-1-0 libxdo3` with apt (the base image is not changed, so
+   a package missing from a future `.deb` `Depends` stays visible) and copies the binary to
+   `~/memry-tauri/`. Rosetta is not used.
+4. **Launch.** `winvm.sh launch-tauri [vault-template]` / `linvm.sh launch-tauri [vault-template]`
+   writes the control file (`control-9222.json` in the guest's temp dir) with dirs under
+   `C:\Users\agent\memry-tauri-data` / `~/memry-tauri-data`, a device `e2e-vm-<uuid>` and a copy of
+   the test vault (or of the template), starts the app with `MEMRY_E2E=1` and
+   `TAURI_WEBDRIVER_PORT=9222` in the console session, tunnels 9222 and waits for `/status`. The
+   real profile is never touched.
+5. **Drive.** `winvm.sh cdp text|shot|eval|run` is routed to `apps/desktop-tauri/scripts/wd.mjs`
+   after `launch-tauri` (WebDriver through `pw-compat`, so `run` scripts get a Playwright-style
+   `{ page, browser }` and the UI recipes below keep working). Run `pnpm install` in the repo
+   first; `wd.mjs` runs under `node --import tsx` from `apps/desktop-tauri`. The `webdriver-memry`
+   MCP server can use the tunnel too: `MEMRY_WEBDRIVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port>`. No main-process
